# Vite reads this for `npm run build`, which is what `npm run dist` ships.
#
# The demo licence hands any device that asks seven days of every paid
# feature, signs the token with the secret this build already carries, and
# counts "once" in a file in the app's own data directory. That is the right
# trade for an internal build, a demonstration, or a reviewer — and the wrong
# one for a release that is also selling subscriptions, so a release turns it
# off. See electron/demo-license.js for the whole argument.
#
# Development builds and the test suites do not read this file, so the entry
# is there without anyone configuring it. To try a production build *with*
# the demo, build with VITE_DISABLE_DEMO_LICENSE=false in the environment,
# which overrides what is here.
#
# This file is Vite's, so it only configures the bundle — it removes the
# entry from the interface. The main process is what actually mints the
# token, and it refuses independently: a packaged app issues no demo licence
# unless its environment also says ENABLE_DEMO_LICENSE=true (see
# `demoAvailable` in electron/main.js). Hiding the button is not the limit.
VITE_DISABLE_DEMO_LICENSE=true
